     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1: Scale 3 [Up to greater extent SDGs integrated in the mandate of existing coordination structures and new structures established. In 2022, the project continued supporting these structures and in providing periodic updates on provincial SDG progress]. 
1.2: Scale 3 [SDG Action plan/frameworks at national/sub-national level established, and development plans are partially SDGs aligned. In 2022, for sub-national planning the project prepared 4 district localization plans for Khyber, Mardan, Upper Dir and Bannu and sectoral policies for 3 priority sectors namely Education, Health and Energy]. 
1.3: Scale 3 [Decent understanding regarding the SDGs have been developed over a period. In 2022, the project focused at creating awareness amongst students by organizing awareness sessions at universities, and within public sector through awareness sessions for district officials and for Bureau of Statistics]. 
1.4: Scale 3 [No target for 2022]. 
2.1: Scale 3 [In 2022, the baselines for more than 100 indicators were updated on BOS Khyber Pakhtunkhwa portal. The project also facilitated review of regional accounts for the estimation of trade sector computation to GDP]. 
2.2: Scale 3 [Reasonable understanding and knowledge on SDGs monitoring and reporting has been established by the project since inception]. 
3.1: Scale 2 [Performance based criteria established but not fully used for resource allocation at national/ sub-national level. In 2022, the project computed financial cost of achieving High-Priority Short-Term SDG targets in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa. 
